{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q21098966","formula":"C₂₁H₃₀O₂","hill":"C21H30O2","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":21.0,"H":30.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Retroprogesterone"},"descriptions":{"en":"Retroprogesterone, also known as 9β,10α-progesterone or as 9β,10α-pregn-4-ene-3,20-dione, is a progestin which was never marketed. It is a stereoisomer of the naturally occurring progestogen progesterone, in which the hydrogen atom at the 9th carbon is in the α-position (below the plane) instead of the β-position (above the plane) and the methyl group at the 10th carbon is in the β-position instead of the α-position. In other words, the atom positions at the two carbons have been reversed relative to progesterone, hence the name retroprogesterone."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":92940,"mass":314.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(=O)[C@H]1CC[C@@H]2[C@@]1(CC[C@@H]3[C@H]2CCC4=CC(=O)CC[C@@]34C)C","inchikey":"RJKFOVLPORLFTN-HQZYFCCVSA-N","iupac":"(8S,9R,10S,13S,14S,17S)-17-acetyl-10,13-dimethyl-1,2,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-dodecahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"92940","atoms":53,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-5.534,"y":-0.129,"z":0.332,"el":"O"},{"x":6.144,"y":-0.443,"z":-0.521,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.331,"y":0.915,"z":-0.249,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.263,"y":-0.187,"z":0.279,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.08,"y":1.135,"z":0.607,"el":"C"},{"x":0.71,"y":-0.196,"z":0.89,"el":"C"},{"x":1.985,"y":-0.397,"z":-0.022,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.41,"y":-0.069,"z":-0.751,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.481,"y":-1.5,"z":0.209,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.206,"y":-1.446,"z":1.06,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.271,"y":2.099,"z":-0.469,"el":"C"},{"x":0.792,"y":2.247,"z":-0.003,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.573,"y":1.449,"z":-0.967,"el":"C"},{"x":2.882,"y":0.844,"z":0.095,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.777,"y":0.062,"z":1.72,"el":"C"},{"x":2.23